From: Alex Deucher <alexander.deucher@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:46:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu/gmc12: properly pass flush_type to
 gmc_v12_0_flush_vm_hub()
References: bsc#1012628
Patch-mainline: 7.2.10
Git-commit: 0bfb1bfc82e8fa386d4fad1caa5812b6afafa626

commit 0bfb1bfc82e8fa386d4fad1caa5812b6afafa626 upstream.

In gmc_v12_0_flush_gpu_tlb(), flush_type was not properly
passed to gmc_v12_0_flush_vm_hub().  This only affected
the MMIO path.  In most cases the flush would go through
MES.

Reviewed-by: Mukul Joshi <mukul.joshi@amd.com>
Signed-off-by: Alex Deucher <alexander.deucher@amd.com>
(cherry picked from commit 6498e33f22a12fdc759a0c78bfe0547819277a36)
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Signed-off-by: Jiri Slaby <jslaby@suse.cz>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v12_0.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v12_0.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v12_0.c
index 84c93364d220..0fc0c783b1cc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v12_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v12_0.c
@@ -327,7 +327,7 @@ static void gmc_v12_0_flush_gpu_tlb(struct amdgpu_device *adev, uint32_t vmid,
 		return;
 	}
 
-	gmc_v12_0_flush_vm_hub(adev, vmid, vmhub, 0);
+	gmc_v12_0_flush_vm_hub(adev, vmid, vmhub, flush_type);
 	return;
 }
 
-- 
2.55.0

